Traffix – Smart Traffic Signal Optimizer
=========================================

Project Overview
----------------
Traffix is a Python-based web application for optimizing traffic signals using AI and real-time data. It provides a web interface for user registration, login, dashboard, intersection management, and traffic analysis using video/image uploads or live feeds.

Frameworks and Libraries Used
----------------------------
- Flask: Main web framework for routing, templating, and session management.
- Werkzeug: Security utilities (password hashing) and file handling.
- Jinja2: Templating engine (via Flask) for rendering HTML pages.
- Firebase Admin SDK: User authentication, Firestore access, and backend data management.
- OpenCV (cv2): Image and video processing.
- Ultralytics YOLO: Vehicle detection using deep learning (YOLOv8 model).
- NumPy: Numerical operations, especially image decoding.
- Torch & Torchvision: Backend for running YOLO models.
- Pillow: Image processing.

Project Structure & Main Modules
-------------------------------
- app.py: Main Flask application. Handles all routes, user authentication, intersection management, traffic analysis, and integrates all modules.
- signal_optimizer.py: Logic for optimizing traffic signal timings based on detected vehicle counts and priorities.
- traffic_detector.py: Uses YOLOv8 to detect vehicles in images and videos, returning vehicle counts and density levels.
- templates/: Jinja2 HTML templates for all web pages.
- static/: Static assets (CSS, JS, images, uploaded videos).
- data/: Legacy local JSON files retained only for one-time migration into Firebase Firestore.
- requirements.txt: Python dependencies.

How Everything Works
-------------------
1. User Authentication
   - Registration/Login: Users register and log in via Flask routes. Credentials are managed using Firebase Authentication.
   - Session Management: Flask sessions track logged-in users.
2. Intersection & Lane Management
   - Each intersection has multiple lanes, each with a direction and a camera.
   - Intersection records are stored in Firebase Firestore. Cameras have unique IDs and can be toggled on/off.
3. Traffic Detection
   - Image/Video Uploads: Users upload lane images or videos for analysis.
   - Live Analysis: Supports live camera feeds (base64 images).
   - Detection: YOLOv8 detects vehicles, returning counts and density levels.
4. Signal Optimization
   - Algorithm: Calculates optimal green light durations for each direction based on vehicle counts and priorities.
   - Adaptive Timing: Distributes total cycle time among lanes, ensuring min/max green times.
5. Dashboard & Analytics
   - Dashboard: Shows intersection stats, camera health, recent analyses, and alerts.
   - Analytics: Tracks traffic history, computes trends, busiest lanes, and provides insights.
6. Data Persistence
   - Users/Profile Metadata: Firebase Firestore (`users` collection)
   - Intersections: Firebase Firestore (`intersections` collection)
   - Traffic History: Firebase Firestore (`traffic_history` collection)
   - Intersection Media Metadata: Firebase Firestore (`intersection_media` collection)
   - Media Files: Uploaded videos/images in static/uploads/lane_videos/
   - Legacy Migration: Existing JSON files in `data/` are imported into Firestore automatically when first accessed.
7. Frontend
   - Templates: HTML pages rendered with Jinja2.
   - Static JS/CSS: Handles UI, authentication, and webcam integration.

Key Features
------------
- User registration/login with Firebase.
- Add/manage intersections and lanes.
- Upload images/videos or use live feeds for traffic analysis.
- AI-based vehicle detection (YOLOv8).
- Adaptive signal timing optimization.
- Dashboard with real-time stats and analytics.
- Cloud-backed data persistence using Firebase Firestore.

Summary Table
-------------
| Area            | Technology/Module         | Purpose                            |
|-----------------|--------------------------|------------------------------------|
| Web Framework   | Flask                    | Routing, sessions, templates       |
| Auth            | Firebase Admin SDK       | User registration/login            |
| AI/Detection    | Ultralytics YOLO, OpenCV | Vehicle detection in images/videos |
| Optimization    | signal_optimizer.py      | Adaptive signal timing             |
| Data Storage    | Firebase Firestore       | Users, intersections, history      |
| Frontend        | Jinja2, HTML, JS, CSS    | User interface                     |
